From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000016 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xxxvik-xakerxxx <19531907+xxxvik-xakerxxx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 17:10:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sysfb: keep damage-limited Tetris I/O updates

The I/O framebuffer quirk currently promotes every atomic damage update to
a full 1080x2400 copy.  That writes 10 MiB to the active bootloader scanout
even when the compositor changed only a small rectangle, and sustained
compositor updates corrupt the physical display while fbcon remains stable.

Keep the write-combined I/O mapping and memcpy_toio path, but let the DRM
damage helper copy only the rectangles supplied by the atomic commit.  This
does not change the framebuffer address, stride, format or bootloader display
state.

Signed-off-by: xxxvik-xakerxxx <19531907+xxxvik-xakerxxx@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/sysfb/simpledrm.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sysfb/simpledrm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sysfb/simpledrm.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sysfb/simpledrm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sysfb/simpledrm.c
@@ -682,7 +682,6 @@ static struct simpledrm_device *simpledrm_device_create(struct drm_driver *drv,
 	sysfb->fb_pitch = stride;
 	sysfb->force_iomem_updates = of_node &&
 		of_property_read_bool(of_node, "linux,force-iomem-updates");
-	sysfb->force_full_frame_updates = sysfb->force_iomem_updates;
 
 	drm_dbg(dev, "display mode={" DRM_MODE_FMT "}\n", DRM_MODE_ARG(&sysfb->fb_mode));
 	drm_dbg(dev, "framebuffer format=%p4cc, size=%dx%d, stride=%d byte\n",
-- 
